# SeleniumForBeginnners

Beginner Selenium WebDriver automation project targeting [practicetestautomation.com](https://practicetestautomation.com). Uses Page Object Model (POM) with TestNG.

## Stack

- Java 21, Maven
- Selenium Java 4.38.0
- TestNG 7.11.0
- Browsers: Chrome (default), Firefox, Chrome headless (`chromeheadless`)

## Layout

```
src/main/java/com/practicetestautomation/baseobjects/   # Page objects
src/test/java/com/practicetestautomation/tests/         # Tests + BaseTest
src/test/resources/TestSuites/                          # TestNG XML suites
```

## Patterns

- **BasePage** — shared `WebDriver`/`WebDriverWait` (10s), `visit()`, visibility/hidden helpers. All page objects extend it.
- **BaseTest** — `@BeforeMethod` creates driver from `@Parameters("browser")`; `@AfterMethod` quits. All test classes extend it.
- Page objects hold `By` locators privately; expose action methods. Login flow returns next page object (e.g. `executeLogin()` → `SuccessfulLoginPage`).
- Tests use `java.util.logging.Logger` via `logger` from `BaseTest`.

## Page objects & target URLs

| Class | URL path |
|-------|----------|
| `LoginPage` | `/practice-test-login/` |
| `SuccessfulLoginPage` | post-login success page |
| `ExceptionPage` | `/practice-test-exceptions/` |

Valid login: `student` / `Password123`.

## Running tests

Default suite: `FullRegressionSuite.xml` (set in `pom.xml`).

```bash
mvn test
mvn test -DsuiteXmlFile=SmokeTestingSuite.xml
mvn test -DsuiteXmlFile=DebugSuite.xml
```

Suites: `SmokeTestingSuite` (smoke group), `FullRegressionSuite` (login + exceptions, multi-browser), `DebugSuite` (single-method runs).

TestNG groups: `smoke`, `positive`, `negative`, `regression`. Negative login tests receive `username`, `password`, `expectedErrorMessage` via suite XML parameters.

## Conventions for changes

- New pages → `baseobjects/`, extend `BasePage`, constructor calls `super(driver)`.
- New tests → `tests/<feature>/`, extend `BaseTest`, register in a suite XML.
- Keep locator strings in page objects, not in tests.
- Match existing style: minimal abstraction, no extra frameworks (no WebDriverManager, no Allure, no Cucumber).
